cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below and also cite the Kvasir datasets (see README)."
title: "ACPolyp: active-contour-guided polyp classification study on Kvasir v2"
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: "Reddy"
    given-names: "P. Vishnu Vardhan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-9605-6739"
    affiliation: "Dept. of Computer Science and Engineering, Amrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham, Bangalore Campus"
  - family-names: "Reddy"
    given-names: "V. Guru Puneeth"
    affiliation: "Dept. of Computer Science and Engineering, Amrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham, Bangalore Campus"
  - family-names: "Reddy"
    given-names: "D. Greeshmanth"
    affiliation: "Dept. of Computer Science and Engineering, Amrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham, Bangalore Campus"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pvishnu318/acpolyp"
abstract: >-
  A leakage-audited, shortcut-aware, statistically controlled study of whether an unsupervised
  active-contour prior improves deep classification of endoscopic findings on Kvasir v2, with a
  calibrated, conformal, explainable inference stack. Research prototype, not a medical device.
  The main finding is a null result: no statistically supported gain from contour guidance.
keywords:
  - polyp classification
  - active contours
  - Kvasir
  - endoscopy
  - conformal prediction
  - reproducibility
